{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronTwoBodyKernel","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronTwoBodyKernel","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.SpecialFunctions.Log.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.ExponentialBounds","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Positivity","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.GCongr"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.no_flavour_split_rescue","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.no_flavour_split_rescue","kind":"theorem","line":408,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronTwoBodyKernel.lean#L408-L430","doc":"**The flavour split cannot rescue the deuteron.**\n\nThe derived colour weight sits within `δ/4 < 3.5 × 10⁻⁴` of the bar-symmetric\nvalue `½`; any weight reproducing a deuteron binding of at most `2.4 MeV` lies\nat or below `0.4`, i.e. at least `0.0996` below balance.  The departure the\ndeuteron demands therefore exceeds `250 ×` the entire derived flavour split.\n\nThis is the sharp form of the negative.  The p–n colour weighting is a\n`10⁻³`-scale structure and the deuteron gap is a `10⁻¹`-scale one, so no\nrefinement of `δ` — subleading corrections included — reaches it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.derived_weight_near_balanced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.derived_weight_near_balanced","kind":"theorem","line":395,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronTwoBodyKernel.lean#L395-L406","doc":"**The derived colour weight is bar-balanced to one part in a thousand.**\n\n`t = ½ − δ(q)/4 ∈ [0.4996, ½]` on the proton-pin interval: the\n`bring_color_weighted` convention displaces the p–n interface from the\nbar-symmetric superposition by less than `3.5 × 10⁻⁴`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.flavorDelta_small","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.flavorDelta_small","kind":"theorem","line":374,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronTwoBodyKernel.lean#L374-L393","doc":"The derived weight `t = ½ − δ(q)/4` is near-balanced: on the proton-pin\ninterval `δ(q)/4 < 3.45 × 10⁻⁴`, so `t ≥ 0.4996`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.required_weight_far_from_balanced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.required_weight_far_from_balanced","kind":"theorem","line":323,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronTwoBodyKernel.lean#L323-L370","doc":"**Any colour weight reproducing a deuteron binding of at most `2.4 MeV`\nlies at or below `0.4`.**\n\nContrapositive of the same bounding chain evaluated at `t = 0.4`, where the\nbond energy is already `≥ 2.547 MeV`.  Since `B_AME(²H) = 2.2246 < 2.4`, the\nexperimental deuteron is reachable in this family only at `t ≤ 0.4` — a\ndeparture of at least `0.0996` from the bar-symmetric weight `½`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.deuteron_overbinds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.deuteron_overbinds","kind":"theorem","line":304,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronTwoBodyKernel.lean#L304-L319","doc":"**The two-body Markov-trace kernel over-binds the deuteron by more than\n25 %.**\n\nStated at the canonical proton pin `q₀ ∈ [1.1099785, 1.1099786]` and CODATA\n`mₑ ∈ [0.5109989, 0.5109990]`, for any near-balanced colour weight.  The\nmeasured value is `+27.34 %`; `1.25` is the margin that survives the rational\nbounding chain above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.overshoot_core","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.overshoot_core","kind":"theorem","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronTwoBodyKernel.lean#L251-L302","doc":"**Numerical core of the deuteron overshoot.**\n\nFor a Markov parameter, skein parameter and energy unit inside the intervals\nthat the proton-pinned substrate and CODATA `mₑ` actually determine, and for\n**any** near-balanced colour weight `t ∈ [0.499, ½]`, the two-body bond energy\nexceeds `1.25 ×` the experimental deuteron binding.\n\nThe bound is proved through the rational chain\n\n  `f ≤ 0.5083671`,\n  `−log f ≥ log 2 + 1 − 2f ≥ 0.6764130`,\n  `(½ − t)·log(1 − h) ≥ 0.001 · (1 − (1 − h)⁻¹) ≥ −0.0002644`,\n  `E · L ≥ 4.185980 × 0.6761486 = 2.83034 > 2.78071 = 1.25 × 2.2245666`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.bondL_strictMono","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.bondL_strictMono","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronTwoBodyKernel.lean#L221-L243","doc":"**The bond energy is strictly increasing in the colour weight `t`.**\n\nBoth terms increase with `t`: the interface factor `z − h·t` decreases (so\n`−log` of it increases), and `−(t − ½)·log(1 − h)` increases because\n`log(1 − h) < 0`.  Consequently the admissible interface family is swept\nmonotonically, `t = 0` (p–p) is its minimum and `t = 1` (n–n) its maximum, and\na bound at one weight bounds every weight on that side. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.bondL_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.bondL_half","kind":"theorem","line":213,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronTwoBodyKernel.lean#L213-L217","doc":"The writhe factor is exactly trivial at the bar-symmetric weight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.interfaceFactor_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.interfaceFactor_half","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronTwoBodyKernel.lean#L197-L211","doc":"**The bar-symmetric p–n interface factor has a closed rational form.**\n\nAt the bar-symmetric weight `t = ½` the writhe exponent `Δe = 2t − 1` vanishes,\nso the writhe factor is exactly `1` and the entire bond energy is\n`E₀ · log(1 / f)` with\n\n  `f = z_D(q) − h(q)/2 = (q⁴+1) / (2q(q²+1))`.\n\nEvery constant on the right-hand side is fixed: there is no scale, no\nnormalisation and no fitted coefficient anywhere in it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.log_ge_one_sub_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.log_ge_one_sub_inv","kind":"theorem","line":189,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronTwoBodyKernel.lean#L189-L193","doc":"`log x ≥ 1 − x⁻¹` for `x > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.neg_log_lower","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.neg_log_lower","kind":"theorem","line":181,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronTwoBodyKernel.lean#L181-L187","doc":"`−log x ≥ log 2 + 1 − 2x` for `x > 0`.  Tight near `x = ½`, which is where\nthe deuteron interface factor sits — the bound loses only `1.7 × 10⁻⁴` there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.BSymDeuteron","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.BSymDeuteron","kind":"def","line":173,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronTwoBodyKernel.lean#L173-L174","doc":"The two-body deuteron binding `B_sym(²H) = E₀ · L(q,t)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.bondL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.bondL","kind":"def","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronTwoBodyKernel.lean#L164-L171","doc":"Writhe-normalised per-bond log-suppression\n`L(q,t) = −log f(q,t) − (t − ½)·log(1 − h(q))`.\n\nThe second term is the writhe normalisation `(1−h)^(Δe/2)` forced by Markov\ninvariance (`QOU.QBeta.WritheNormalisation`, sorry-free, unique up to sign);\nfor the colour superposition the exponent-sum expectation is `Δe = 2t − 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.E0","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.E0","kind":"def","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronTwoBodyKernel.lean#L160-L162","doc":"The CAL-1 × CAL-2 energy unit `E₀ = mₑ/(q(q−1))`.  `mₑ` is CAL-1 (it fixes\nthe MeV scale); `q` is pinned by CAL-2 through its proton proxy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.tDerived","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.tDerived","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronTwoBodyKernel.lean#L156-L158","doc":"The derived colour weight `t = ½ − δ(q)/4` (`bring_color_weighted`,\nowner ruling R3, 2026-08-15). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.interfaceFactor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.interfaceFactor","kind":"def","line":147,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronTwoBodyKernel.lean#L147-L154","doc":"Interface factor of the p–n bond at colour weight `t`:\n`f(q,t) = z_D(q) − h(q)·t`.\n\n`t` is the weight of the `σ⁻¹` branch in the superposition `(1−t)·σ + t·σ⁻¹`;\nusing the Hecke skein relation `σ⁻¹ = σ − h·1` this superposition is\n`σ − h·t·1`, so `t` is exactly the scalar dressing in units of `−h`.\n`t = 0` is the p–p bond (`σ`), `t = 1` the n–n bond (`σ⁻¹`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.flavorDelta","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.flavorDelta","kind":"def","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronTwoBodyKernel.lean#L143-L145","doc":"Leading flavour split `δ(q) = (q−1)²·(1 − q⁻⁴)/3`\n(`prop:flavor-split-substrate`, `_li_2_q_util.flavor_split_leading`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.hq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.hq","kind":"def","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronTwoBodyKernel.lean#L140-L141","doc":"Hecke skein parameter `h(q) = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.zD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.DeuteronKernel.zD","kind":"def","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/DeuteronTwoBodyKernel.lean#L136-L138","doc":"**Convention-D** Markov parameter `z_D(q) = q³/(q²+1)` (owner ruling R1,\n2026-08-15).  NOT the excised convention-C `√q/(q+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}